  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/338887.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 168px;\" /><br />Neopentyl bromide give a carbocation as intermediate which undergo for rearrangement and show <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mtext>1</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> mechanism (even though it has no <math> <mrow> <mtext>β</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>H</mtext></mrow> </math> atom).<br /><br />Thus Rearrangement of carbocations by <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>E</mtext>   <mtext>1</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math> mechanism is the correct option.",
